### Local smoke requests (VS / Rider / VS Code REST Client).
### Tokens come from the OAuth 2.0 device authorization grant (RFC 8628); there is no password grant.
### Shortcut: `./scripts/get-token.ps1 -Scope "catalog.write identity.write platform.ops"` and paste the token below.
@host = http://localhost:5080
@keycloak = http://localhost:8080/realms/modular-monolith

### 1) Request a device code. Default scopes: catalog.read, identity.read; the write and operator scopes are optional.
# @name device
POST {{keycloak}}/protocol/openid-connect/auth/device
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id=modular-monolith-cli&scope=openid%20catalog.write%20identity.write%20platform.ops

### 2) Open the "verification_uri_complete" of the response in a browser and sign in, e.g. as alice
###    (tenant "acme", roles admin + operator; enrol an authenticator app at the first login).
### 3) Exchange the approved device code for tokens.
# @name token
POST {{keycloak}}/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:device_code&client_id=modular-monolith-cli&device_code={{device.response.body.device_code}}

###
@accessToken = {{token.response.body.access_token}}

### Register the caller's profile (publishes UserRegisteredIntegrationEvent -> Catalog sellers)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/identity/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: register-alice-1

{ "email": "alice@acme.test", "displayName": "Alice" }

### Create a product (idempotent)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/catalog/products
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: create-widget-1

{ "name": "Widget", "sku": "WID-001", "price": 19.99, "currency": "USD" }

### List products of the caller's tenant (paged: page >= 1, 1 <= pageSize <= 100)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/catalog/products?page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Get one product (use the id from the Location header of the create call); note its "version"
@productId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
GET {{host}}/api/v1/catalog/products/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Conditional GET: repeat with the ETag you received -> 304 Not Modified
GET {{host}}/api/v1/catalog/products/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
If-None-Match: "1-0000000000000000"

### Change the price with If-Match (preferred). A stale ETag returns 412, no precondition returns 428.
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/catalog/products/{{productId}}/price
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: "1-0000000000000000"

{ "price": 24.99, "currency": "USD" }

### ...or with the version in the body (a stale version returns 409)
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/catalog/products/{{productId}}/price
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "price": 26.99, "currency": "USD", "version": 2 }

### Price in another currency (output-cached per tenant for Modules:Catalog:PriceOutputCacheSeconds)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/catalog/products/{{productId}}/price?currency=EUR
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Operators (role operator + scope platform.ops): inspect and replay dead-lettered outbox messages
GET {{host}}/api/v1/ops/outbox/catalog/dead-letters?page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
POST {{host}}/api/v1/ops/outbox/catalog/dead-letters/requeue
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Personal data: export everything the application stores about the caller (GDPR Art. 15/20)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/privacy/me/personal-data
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Personal data: erase the caller's profile (Identity at once, other modules via identity.user-erased)
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/identity/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Tenant admins: erase another user of the tenant by subject id
@subjectId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/identity/users/{{subjectId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Health and metrics (anonymous)
GET {{host}}/health/ready

###
GET {{host}}/metrics
